[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":35},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-7,"_20":21,"_22":-7,"_23":-7,"_24":25},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":32,"_13":33,"_30":34},"id","centros","nome","Centers","rascunho",false,"html","<p>With the 1st layer on the bottom and the whole top face yellow, only the 4 side centers are left. The corners are already in place, so the algorithms in this step only swap centers. There are two cases, made of <a href=\"/en/glossary#sledgehammer\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two triggers: the sledgehammer is R' F R F' and the hedgeslammer, F R' F' R. On the Skewb, they make up almost every algorithm in Sarah's…\">sledgehammers</a> (R&#39; F R F&#39;) and hedgeslammers (F R&#39; F&#39; R).</p>\n<h2>One center right: the other 3 cycle</h2>\n<p>Hold it with the right center at the back. Look at the front center: it has the color of one of the sides.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/fb43ac7c72870864.svg\" alt=\"The back center is right and the front one has the left color (red): `(R' F R F') y (R' F R F') y2 (R' F R F') y (F R' F' R)`.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The back center is right and the front one has the left color (red): <code>(R&#39; F R F&#39;) y (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y2 (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y (F R&#39; F&#39; R)</code>.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/f2fe1aa0584d05b3.svg\" alt=\"The back center is right and the front one has the right color (orange): `(R' F R F') y' (R' F R F') y2 (R' F R F') y' (F R' F' R)`.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The back center is right and the front one has the right color (orange): <code>(R&#39; F R F&#39;) y&#39; (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y2 (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y&#39; (F R&#39; F&#39; R)</code>.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The front one has the left color:</strong> <code>(R&#39; F R F&#39;) y (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y2 (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y (F R&#39; F&#39; R)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>The front one has the right color:</strong> <code>(R&#39; F R F&#39;) y&#39; (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y2 (R&#39; F R F&#39;) y&#39; (F R&#39; F&#39; R)</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>None right: opposites swapped</h2>\n<p>If the front has the back color and the right has the left one, the opposite centers are swapped. One algorithm solves it:</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/68374988607342f2.svg\" alt=\"The opposite centers swapped: `(R' F R F') y2 (F R' F' R) y2 (R' F R F')`.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The opposite centers swapped: <code>(R&#39; F R F&#39;) y2 (F R&#39; F&#39; R) y2 (R&#39; F R F&#39;)</code>.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>If no center is right and the opposites aren&#39;t swapped, do the 3-center algorithm with any center at the back: one of the cases above is left.</p>\n<h2>Next</h2>\n<p>The Skewb is solved. To go faster, <a href=\"/en/skewb/sarah-advanced\">Sarah&#39;s Advanced</a> does the top face and the centers at once.</p>\n","treino","metodos",[26],"anterior","proximo","grupos",[],{"_13":27,"_28":29,"_30":31},"Sarah's Intermediate","numero",3,"endereco","/skewb/sarah#centros","skewb","Skewb","/skewb/",{"_36":37,"_38":39},"cubos",[42,43,44,45,46,47,48],"idiomas",[40,41],"pt","en",{"_11":56,"_13":56},{"_11":55,"_13":55},{"_11":54,"_13":54},{"_11":53,"_13":53},{"_11":51,"_13":52},{"_11":49,"_13":50},{"_11":32,"_13":33},"pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","2x2","3x3"]
